<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Cemenco lifts full yr shr, div falls.</title>
<headline>Cemenco lifts full yr shr, div falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib   (cts)   51.80     vs  35.40</p>
<p>    - pre-excepts (cts)   50.60     vs  (1.20)</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 12.50     vs  26.50</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    4.63     vs   3.17</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   11.70     vs   8.08</p>
<p>    Tax			  7.05     vs   4.90</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    5.87     vs   3.49</p>
<p>    Turnover		 549.60     vs 407.09</p>
<p>Full name: The Cementation Company (Africa) Ltd</p>
<p>(industrial-engineering)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	0.11     vs   3.42</p>
<p>NOTE - The directors have resolved not to proceed with the capitalisation share award of ordinary shares to shareholders previously announced on December 24. This follows a review which revealed that certain internal controls and accounting procedures were circumvented by management members of the group's subsidiary Efco Furnaces, resulting in an overstatement of certain accounts.</p>
<p>The company said it expected to return to reasonable levels of profitability in the year ahead. The level of ordinary dividends which would be declared next year would depend on profitability and future cash flows.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
